kely this has gone last week i told  you it was two to one in favor of  democrats it is now two and a third or  you know whatever it's it's well beyond  two to one at this point in time and  again  these are numbers that have improved for  democrats uh there was a point in early  june where democrats had a 40  shot of holding the senate that is now a  70 shot  very very important to understand  because there are people writing to me  saying david why do you keep saying  democrats are going to have 70 senators  and of course david is not saying that  what i am telling you is that it is a 70  chance  that democrats hold the senate the most  likely outcome  is that democrats hold it  51 to 49 that would be a gain of one  seat right now in the senate it's 50 50.  the vice president gets a tie-breaking  vote that's kamala harris so democrats  are in the majority  50 50 plus kamala the most likely  outcome here is a 51 to 49 majority for  democrats so please do not write to me  saying david democrats have no chance in  hell of getting 70 seats  i'm agreeing with you that's not what  the number means that's not what the  number means  but i appreciate everybody writing in so  the bottom line  democrats chances continuing to improve  and if they merely continue improving at  the same rate  the house will end up a 50-50 flip of  the coin by early november we will watch  and see whether that happens

